    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493309992/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Sunday, October 26. 1902.. Gazzada
We have been here several days, with Don Guido and Donna Carmelita and the ladies Gropallo.
I am sorry I did not write all summer. But B.B. was ill, tired nearly to death, Alys was ill (nervous break-down), Gertrude Morton weighed terribly on my mind, and somehow I lacked spirits to do anything for myself.
We had nice visits from Senda’s friend Miss Adeline Moffat, from Emery Walker, a long visit from that detestably unselfish saint, Zangwill, and many visits from Britten - besides the Trevys, Mr. Dell, Mrs. Crawford, Percy Feilding, """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 63 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1902-03> .

